  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "The 2026 Men's NCAA Tournament culminates with the Final Four at Lucas Oil Stadium in Indianapolis on April 4 and 6. The tournament opens with the First Four in Dayton, Ohio, on March 17-18. Other host sites include Buffalo, Greenville, Oklahoma City, Portland, Tampa, Philadelphia, San Diego, and St. Louis, with regionals in Houston, San Jose, Chicago, and D.C.. Men's NCAA Tournament 2026 Key Locations First Four: UD Arena, Dayton, Ohio (March 17-18) First & Second Rounds: Buffalo, Greenville, Oklahoma City, Portland, Tampa (Benchmark International Arena), Philadelphia (Wells Fargo Center), San Diego (Viejas Arena), St. Louis (Enterprise Center) Regionals (Sweet 16/Elite Eight): Houston (Toyota Center), San Jose (SAP Center), Chicago (United Center), Washington D.C. (Capital One Arena) Final Four: Lucas Oil Stadium, Indianapolis, Indiana (April 4 & 6) Future Men's Final Four Locations 2027: Detroit (Ford Field) 2028: Las Vegas (Allegiant Stadium) 2029: Indianapolis (Lucas Oil Stadium) 2030: North Texas (AT&T Stadium) 2031: Atlanta (Mercedes-Benz Stadium) Women's Final Four Locations 2026: Phoenix, AZ (Mortgage Matchup Center) 2027: Columbus, OH (Nationwide Arena) 2028: Indianapolis (Gainbridge Fieldhouse) 2029: San Antonio, TX (Alamodome)",
